From 5bc5335dc0b319f86f6f8fc2cf263f8236015806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Perjan Smulders <perjan.smulders@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:03:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B device profile

Adds a profile for the Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B, a 7" 1024x600
ESP32-P4 board with an ESP32-C6 WiFi co-processor.

- devices/waveshare-esp32-p4-wifi6-touch-lcd-7b: based on the JC1060P470
  profile, using ESPHome's bundled WAVESHARE-ESP32-P4-WIFI6-TOUCH-LCD-7B
  display model, backlight on GPIO32 (active low), GT911 touch on the
  shared I2C bus, production (rev 3.x) ESP32-P4 silicon, WiFi only
- the panel is mounted upright, so the profile overrides the shared
  1024x600 display profile's 180-degree display offset to 0
- builds, product model, compatibility fixtures, docs page, install
  selector and slug lists; regenerated outputs via npm run prepare:ci
- check_web_smoke.js now reads each device's own features block, so a
  device whose display offset differs from the first device is checked
  correctly

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
