+---
+title: "Waveshare ESP32-P4 7B Home Assistant Setup"
+description:
+  EspControl on the Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B - a 7-inch 1024x600 landscape touchscreen with 15 cards, powered by ESP32-P4.
+---
+
+# 7-inch Waveshare ESP32-P4 7B
+
+The **Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD-7B** is a 7-inch 1024x600 landscape touchscreen powered by an **ESP32-P4**, with an **ESP32-C6** co-processor for WiFi. It uses the same 3x5 EspControl layout as the Guition JC1060P470, but it is a different board with different pins, so it needs its own firmware.
+
+::: warning Community-contributed profile
+This profile compiles in CI but has not yet been confirmed on physical hardware. Please report what works and what does not in a GitHub issue.
+:::
+
+The board has no Ethernet port, so only the WiFi firmware is available. The profile assumes a production ESP32-P4 chip (revision 3.x). If the boot log shows `chip revision: v1.x`, build the firmware yourself with `engineering_sample: true`.
+
+## Card Grid
+
+<!--@include: ../generated/screens/waveshare-p4-7b-grid.md-->
+
+## Install
+
+Connect the display to your computer with a USB-C data cable, then click the button below.
+
+<!--@include: ../generated/screens/waveshare-p4-7b-install.md-->
+
+For WiFi setup and Home Assistant pairing, follow the [Install guide](/getting-started/install).
+
+## ESPHome Manual Setup
+
+```yaml
+substitutions:
+  name: "office-screen"
+  friendly_name: "Office Screen"
+
+wifi:
+  ssid: !secret wifi_ssid
+  password: !secret wifi_password
+
+packages:
+  setup:
+    url: https://github.com/jtenniswood/espcontrol/
+    file: devices/waveshare-esp32-p4-wifi6-touch-lcd-7b/packages.yaml
+    refresh: 1sec
+```
+
